<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="sec" style="background:#FFFFFF">
<div class="in">
<div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:48px 72px;align-items:flex-start">
<div class="stack" style="flex:1 1 300px;min-width:0;gap:20px;max-width:380px" data-reveal>
<h2 class="h2" data-split>Restaurant scheduling, answered</h2>
<p class="txt">Want to see it with your own venues? We'll walk you through Workofo with your data.</p>
</div>
<div class="retail-faq" data-rs-faq style="flex:2 1 520px;min-width:0" data-reveal>
<details><summary>What is restaurant scheduling software?</summary><p>Restaurant scheduling software builds rotas around expected demand instead of last week's pattern. Workofo forecasts workload per location, plans kitchen, bar and floor staff, and applies local labor rules automatically.</p></details>
<details><summary>How does Workofo forecast restaurant demand?</summary><p>It uses promotions, seasonality, weather and local events to predict workload per location, including the busy periods before and after peak service.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can Workofo plan kitchen, bar and floor separately?</summary><p>Yes. Staffing is planned by role, and differences in employee speed and experience are factored in.</p></details>
<details><summary>How does Workofo help with labor cost?</summary><p>Revenue, labor hours and cost of labor % are shown per day next to the rota, so managers see the effect of every change before publishing.</p></details>
<details><summary>What happens when someone calls in sick?</summary><p>Workofo recommends shift changes to cover absences and unexpected demand, so managers don't rebuild the rota by hand.</p></details>
<div class="retail-faq__more" data-rs-faq-more hidden>
<details><summary>Can we share staff between restaurants?</summary><p>Yes. You can move, borrow or lend employee hours between locations when needed.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does Workofo follow local labor rules?</summary><p>Yes. Contracts, rest rules and local agreements are applied to every rota.</p></details>
<details><summary>Do managers stay in charge?</summary><p>Yes. Workofo supports managers, it doesn't replace them. They review, adjust and publish the rota, and can test business rules over time.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is there an app for restaurant staff?</summary><p>Yes. Staff check their rota, set availability and swap shifts in the Workofo mobile app.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does Workofo work for restaurant groups?</summary><p>Yes. Every location is planned in one system, from a single venue to groups with thousands of employees.</p></details>
</div>
<button type="button" class="pill retail-faq-more__toggle" data-rs-faq-toggle aria-expanded="false">
<span class="retail-faq-more__more">Load more questions</span>
<span class="retail-faq-more__less">Show less</span>
<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
</button>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<BottomDemoCta
  demoHref={demoHref}
  headingId="rs-cta-heading"
  title="Book a demo built around your restaurants."
  sub="Show us your venues, roles and rush hours, and we'll show you the rota Workofo would build."
  note="We'll get back to you within one working day."
  tailoredSub="Your venues, roles and rules"
  ariaLabel="Notifications: request received, demo tailored to your restaurants, demo booked."
/>

<script is:inline>
(function () {
  const faq = document.querySelector('[data-rs-faq]');
  if (!faq) return;
  const more = faq.querySelector('[data-rs-faq-more]');
  const btn = faq.querySelector('[data-rs-faq-toggle]');
  if (!more || !btn) return;
  const items = Array.from(more.querySelectorAll('details'));
  function setExpanded(on) {
    faq.classList.toggle('is-expanded', on);
    btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', on ? 'true' : 'false');
    if (on) {
      more.hidden = false;
      items.forEach(function (el, idx) {
        el.setAttribute('data-reveal', '');
        el.classList.remove('is-in');
        window.setTimeout(function () {
          el.classList.add('is-in');
        }, 40 + idx * 70);
      });
    } else {
      more.hidden = true;
      items.forEach(function (el) {
        el.classList.remove('is-in');
        el.removeAttribute('data-reveal');
      });
    }
  }
  btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
    setExpanded(!faq.classList.contains('is-expanded'));
  });
})();
</script>
